      "publication_year": 2020,
      "publication_date": "2020-01-01",
      "abstract": "This chapter builds on the author\u2019s earlier Hegelian critique of Luk\u00e1cs\u2019s philosophy of praxis by construing a conceptual dialogue between Luk\u00e1cs and his one-time mentor, Georg Simmel. It is argued that Luk\u00e1cs\u2019s philosophy in the 1920s was partially formed as a metacritique of Simmel\u2019s absolute relativism, as expressed in \"The Philosophy of Money\". However, Luk\u00e1cs\u2019s alternative generates a conceptual mythology that can be diagnosed in Simmelian terms and sublated by the philosophy of life outlined in \"The View of Life\". By situating it in the present, this may de-reify Luk\u00e1cs\u2019s concept of praxis, allowing it to satisfy its ethical and rational duty.",
